roles.description:
Cigna-Evernorth Services Inc. seeks a Production Support Director for the Bloomfield, CT location to be part of the Global Solutions Group (GSG) Operations team..
Responsibilities:
• Lead functional/technical analysis efforts for resolution of various customer reported issues in mobile and web applications.
• Troubleshoot issues with multiple delivery teams, third party vendors, and clients.
• Create and manage automated scripts for functional monitoring of mobile and web-based applications.
• Liaise between multiple technical teams to resolve problems in complex architecture/designs.
• Provide effective product backlog management and prioritize user stories with business partners.
• Lead and manage daily Scrum and Production Defect Resolution calls, as well as troubleshoot calls.
• Hold primary accountability for all production activities related to GSG applications including myCigna Mobile, Cigna Home Delivery Pharmacy (CHDP), Drug Price Quote Tool (DPQT), PDL Viewer, Cigna Health Assessment, Brand Portal, Media Bin, CGS Customer Portal (CPSE), CGS Admin Portal (BI Admin), Cigna Easy Choice Tool (CECT), Envoy Mobile, Envoy Client Portal, Cigna Virtual Health (CVH), MENA, Centricity, Newsroom, Cigna.com Microsites, Livesite Content Services (LSCS), Content Hub, and Teamsite in the production environment.
• Facilitate communication with delivery teams, driving efficiencies, quick turn-around, and the quality resolution of production defects that impact GSG internal and external customers.
• Hybrid work schedule.

Qualifications:
• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field and 5 years of experience in any healthcare application support role.
• Must have experience with: managing IT production support for web and mobile healthcare applications;
• Ensuring stability and compliance for HIPAA-sensitive systems; Building and managing geographically distributed 24x7 support teams for large-scale digital assets;
• Dynatrace for Real User monitoring, API monitoring, and synthetics; Tealeaf and Discover for real time user analytics;
• Splunk for log indexing, monitoring, and reporting; Implementing automated reporting and dashboards to improve incident visibility and operational efficiency;
• ETL and Databricks job monitoring with alerting, runbook-driven remediation, automated retries/rollbacks, and escalation workflows;
• Incident management including defining Service Level Objectives, categorizing severe incidents, and driving resolution for critical issues;
• Managing production support operations meeting Service Level Agreements for ticket volumes exceeding 1,000 per week across multiple channels including customer calls, app store complaints, opinion labs, and automated monitoring alerts;
